# Web SEO: Blog post body (CMS HTML)

Public posts at `/blog/[slug]` render CMS HTML through `BlogPost.svelte` after `normalizeBlogContentLinks`. Edit in secret-admin **HTML source** (or visual) — do not add a markdown file under `web/src/content` for blog articles.

FAQ, HowTo, and Product blocks are **form fields** (`faq_items`, `howto_steps`, `product`). They render in `BlogPostSeoBlocks` and JSON-LD (`createBlogPostSEOSchema`). Do not duplicate those Q&A / step lists as a second accordion in `content`.

**FAQ answers and How-to step text** use the same Visual / HTML source editor as Content (`BlogRichTextField`). Questions and step **names** stay plain text. Paste root-relative `<a href="/tools/skill-builder">Skill Builder</a>` (or use Visual → link; the prompt keeps `/…` paths). Visible HTML is normalized with `prepareBlogRichTextForDisplay`; JSON-LD `Answer.text` / `HowToStep.text` is **plain text** (`stripHtmlToPlainText`) so schema stays valid.

## Pick the tool page, not the hub

Do **not** send most equity to `/tools`. Link the **specific** tool the article is about.

| Article topic | Primary href | Typical anchors |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Agent skills, `SKILL.md`, zips, CLI recipes, Codex/ChatGPT skills | `/tools/skill-builder` | Skill Builder |
| Same + a named channel | `/tools/skill-builder/{slug}` | TikTok Skill Builder |
| Timing tests / “when to post” (secondary unless the post is about timing) | `/tools/best-time-to-post` or `…/{slug}` | Best Time to Post calculator |
| Stills / covers / aspect ratios | `/tools/photo-editor` or `…/{slug}` | Photo Editor |
| Humanizer / “sound more human” / less machine-written drafts | `/tools/humanizer` or `…/{slug}` | Humanizer |
| Listing several unrelated utilities | `/tools` (at most once) | OpenQuok free tools |

Skills / MCP / CLI how-tos (ChatGPT, Codex, OpenClaw, CapCut + OpenQuok Core) → **Skill Builder is the primary internal tool link**. Mention `/tools` only if you truly mean the whole catalog.

Prefer **one or two** links per destination. Repeat the tool name in prose without linking every mention.

## Internal links (pass equity)

Use **root-relative** paths. The normalizer strips `rel`/`target` on same-site and `/…` hrefs so they stay **dofollow**. Do not add `rel="nofollow"` on internal anchors.

Also link `/docs/…`, `/playbooks`, `/channels/{slug}` when those pages match the sentence. Channel slugs follow `publicChannelConfig` (`tiktok`, `instagram`, …).

```html
<!-- ✅ GOOD — Skill Builder is the destination; hub is not a substitute -->
<p>Assemble <code>openquok-core</code> in <a href="/tools/skill-builder">Skill Builder</a> instead of zipping by hand.</p>
<p>For TikTok recipes, start from the <a href="/tools/skill-builder/tiktok">TikTok Skill Builder</a>.</p>

<!-- ❌ BAD — generic hub when the post is about skills -->
<p>See our <a href="/tools">free tools</a>.</p>
```

Absolute `https://www.openquok.com/…` is treated as internal (followable). Prefer `/tools/skill-builder` (and siblings) so self-host and preview stay same-origin in the editor.

## External links

Third-party `http(s)` get `rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow"` + `target="_blank"` on display. You do not need to hand-author those attributes.

## Checklist (blog HTML)

- [ ] Primary tool link is the matching page (`/tools/skill-builder` for skill posts) — not only `/tools`
- [ ] Channel tool URLs use catalog slugs when a platform is named
- [ ] Headings stay `h2` / `h3` (TipTap); no extra `h1` in the body
- [ ] FAQ answers and How-to steps can include the same internal `<a href="/tools/skill-builder">` links (admin Visual / HTML source)
- [ ] FAQ / HowTo stay in the admin SEO fields, not copied into `content`
